    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d862">

                <pb facs="1087" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.602 Ot 81/197</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to George W. Goethals and
                        Company</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The Department has received your
                    letter of April 28th, addressed to Mr. Dulles, Chief of the Division of Near
                    Eastern Affairs,<anchor n="40" xml:id="d862-f1"/> in which you refer to the
                    Chester project and state that you understand that a history of this project is
                    available in the files of the Department. It is presumed that your letter of
                    inquiry has been written as a result of the visit to the Department of Major K.
                    E. Clayton-Kennedy, a Canadian citizen, who indicated that you were interested
                    in the Chester project and that you were inclined to participate with Admiral
                    Chester, Arthur Chester, Major Kennedy and others to interest American
                    enterprise in the possible establishment and development of rights which were
                    the object of prolonged negotiation with the Ottoman authorities some years
                    ago.</p>
                <p>The Department has no history of the Chester project such as that to which you
                    refer. In view of the voluminous character of the correspondence on this subject
                    and the fact that it relates to the negotiations of private American citizens,
                    it is suggested that you furnish the Department with further details regarding
                    the exact nature of the data which you desire.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leland
                            Harrison</hi>,</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
